REQ-PB-070 title=Implement Template 13 Stakeholder & Adoption Plan as a native register|input_fields=Stakeholder;Impact;Current stance;Required behavior;Intervention;Owner;Adoption KPI|procedure=Users record each stakeholder group; Impact H/M/L; Current stance Support / Neutral / Resist; Intervention Comms / training / involvement / incentive|acceptance=A01: T13 persists all 7 columns; stance 'Hostile' is rejected; Intervention accepts the four source values|final_gate=DG4

REQ-PB-079 title=Implement Template 15 RAID as a native register|input_fields=ID;Type;Description;Impact;Probability;Owner;Due;Mitigation / action;Status|procedure=Users log Risk, Assumption, Issue and Dependency entries (IDs R01, A01, I01, D01); Impact H/M/L; Status Open by default|acceptance=A01: T15 persists all 9 columns; Type outside Risk/Assumption/Issue/Dependency is rejected|final_gate=DG4

REQ-PB-047 title=Implement Template 6 Prioritization Scorecard as a native register|input_fields=Initiative;Strategic fit (25%);Financial value (25%);Customer impact (20%);Feasibility (15%);Time-to-value (15%);Weighted score|procedure=Scorers enter 1-5 per criterion for each initiative; Weighted score is calculated; ranked table shown|acceptance=A01: T06 persists all criteria per initiative; Weighted score is read-only (calculated)|final_gate=DG3

REQ-PB-048 title=Apply T06 default weights 25/25/20/15/15 with a 1-5 scale and a calculated weighted score|input_fields=Strategic fit weight 25%;Financial value weight 25%;Customer impact weight 20%;Feasibility weight 15%;Time-to-value weight 15%;Score 1-5|procedure=Weighted score = sum(score x weight) on the 1-5 scale; scores outside 1-5 rejected; missing score marks the row incomplete|acceptance=A01;A05: scores 5,4,3,2,1 give 3.30 (decimal, exact); a score of 6 is rejected; a missing score shows 'incomplete', not a numeric total|final_gate=DG3

REQ-PB-049 title=Adjust T06 weights per transformation, including risk/compliance replacing part of the weighting, with a 100% total check and versioned weight sets|input_fields=Transformation;Criterion;Weight;Risk/compliance criterion;Weight-set version;Effective from|procedure=Authorized users propose an adjusted weight set for a transformation, optionally with a risk/compliance criterion that replaces part of the weighting; the server rejects any set whose weights do not total 100%; an approved set becomes a new immutable version, earlier versions are kept, and every scoring and ranking records the weight-set version it used|acceptance=A01;A05;A07: saving weights totalling 95% (or 105%) is rejected with a validation error; a risk/compliance criterion at 10% with strategic fit reduced to 15% is accepted as weight-set version 2 and rescoring uses it; scores computed under version 1 keep their version-1 reference; the REQ-S09-005 ranking history can name 'weight version 2' as the cause of a rank change|final_gate=DG3

REQ-PB-050 title=Implement Template 7 Wave Roadmap with the four seeded source waves|input_fields=Wave;Purpose;Typical horizon;Entry criteria;Exit evidence|procedure=Seed Wave 0 — Mobilize (0-6 weeks), Wave 1 — Prove (1-3 months), Wave 2 — Scale (3-9 months), Wave 3 — Embed (6-18 months) with source purpose, entry criteria and exit evidence; initiatives are assigned to waves with dates|acceptance=A01: four waves seeded with values verbatim (e.g. '0-6 weeks', 'Sponsor + charter'); overlapping horizons are accepted|final_gate=DG3

REQ-PB-065 title=Implement Template 11 Decision Rights Matrix with the four seeded source rows|input_fields=Decision;Recommend;Approve;Consult;Inform;SLA|procedure=Seed Business scope change, Funding reallocation, Target-state design and Go-live / scale with source roles and SLAs (5 working days; Next SteerCo / urgent route; 10 working days; Per release plan); approvals route per the matrix|acceptance=A01: four rows seeded verbatim; a change request of type Business scope change routes approval to the Sponsor|final_gate=DG4

REQ-PB-066 title=Compute T11 SLAs by type: working days, next forum or release plan|input_fields=SLA type (working days | Next SteerCo / urgent route | Per release plan);Working days|procedure=Working-day SLAs use the business calendar (Asia/Riyadh default); 'Next SteerCo / urgent route' resolves to the next scheduled SteerCo or an urgent route; 'Per release plan' uses the linked release date|acceptance=A09: a Business scope change raised Thursday gets a due date 5 working days later skipping the configured weekend days and holidays|final_gate=DG4

